[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   Step 083 -- perturber mass ladder: what point mass would the
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   transit anomaly require?
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   step_062 showed that the two published Brown & Batygin (2021)
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   realizations inject <= 0.003 deg of boundary rotation against the
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   >= 0.14 deg observed -- a shortfall of roughly two orders of
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   magnitude in angle.  This step converts that shortfall into a mass
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   statement.  The gravitational impulse a distant perturber delivers to
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   a comet's reconstructed orbit scales with the perturber's mass, so a
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   mass ladder at fixed geometry measures both the scaling exponent and
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   the mass a point-mass explanation would actually require.
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   Cells
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   bb21_med_m7    m9 =   6.9 M_earth (the published realization, M9 = 180)
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   bb21_med_m20   m9 =  20   "
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   bb21_med_m50   m9 =  50   "
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   bb21_med_m150  m9 = 150   "
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   sct25_px       m9 =   4.4 M_earth, a = 290 AU, e = 0.29, i = 6.8 deg --
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   the Siraj, Chyba & Tremaine (2025, ApJ 978, 139)
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   quadrivariate best fit, placed in the anti-aligned
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   shepherding configuration (varpi9 = 246.7, Om9 = 96.9,
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   the same apsidal geometry as bb21_med; the fit
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   constrains m, a, e, i only) at M9 = 180.
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   All cells use the residence-time-weighted most probable position
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   M9 = 180 deg.  The m9 = 6.9 anchor is taken from the step_b27 CSV
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   (deterministic integrator, identical inputs) so each comet needs one
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   no-P9 baseline plus four new integrations.
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   Per comet the periapsis-direction rotation drot is measured at each
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   mass; a log-log fit on the bb21_med ladder gives the scaling exponent
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   alpha (drot ~ m^alpha), and the required mass
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   m_req = 6.9 * (d_of / drot_6.9)^(1/alpha)
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   is the point mass at the published location that would reproduce that
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   comet's observed orig->future rotation d_of.  Deliverables: the
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   scaling exponent, the required-mass distribution in and out of the
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   cap, and the same targeting/absorption statistics as step_062 for the
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   Siraj realization.
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   Context for interpretation (recorded in the JSON): Pan-STARRS1 +
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   ZTF + DES already exclude ~78 per cent of the BB21 parameter space
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   (Brown, Holman & Batygin 2024, AJ 167, 146); IRAS/WISE all-sky limits bound any
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   roughly Jupiter-mass-or-larger body well inside ~10^4 AU; and
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   planetary-ranging ephemerides bound a ~300-500 AU perturber at a few
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   tens of Earth masses.  A required mass of order 10^3-10^4 M_earth is
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   not a planet -- it is a brown dwarf that every relevant survey
[2026-09-21 14:53:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 083]   excludes.
